= Profile, Robot  [RP-nn] =

//For the System itself, not a “Persona.” Covers the equivalent ground as a Human Persona, describing machine capabilities and design intent rather than human-like traits.//

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. RP-01, RP-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained (direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant), flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Design Pattern, cite known uses in other projects or the literature grounding its Principle instead.
|Role in Scenario|its position in the Design Scenario.
|Social Competencies|what kind of exchange it conducts: turn-taking, responsiveness, adaptivity.
|Embodiment|physical form, mobility, sensors, expressive capabilities, and their limits.
|Narrative and Identity Framing|what story or identity it presents to users, and what it deliberately avoids presenting as.
|Communication Strategies|modalities, style, tone, and pacing.
|Privacy and Data Handling|what is processed where, what is retained, and for how long.
|Context-Aware Capabilities|how its behaviour adapts to context, and what is not yet implemented.

== Graph edges ==

realizes → Technology Option (§1.3); addresses → Human Value (§1.2); enables → Function; referenced-by → Value Story.